  "sampling": "Reuse the exact previously frozen indices for paired comparisons. Training and evaluation disjoint within each draw; independent draws may overlap.",
  "training": "Original 8 epochs, batch 128 including remainder, SGD .03/momentum .9/weight decay .0001, approximate-softmax gradient, fixed normalization, mild affine schedules, He-uniform initialization and fresh state per member.",
  "arithmetic": "Original ordered FP32 kernels; new coupling uses separate FP32 multiply/add with no FMA; sum three raw score arrays in seed order",
  "architecture_changes": "Only architecture differs: topology, depth, parameter shapes, and fixed residual scale .25. Random constructor consumption necessarily depends on architecture; seed and He policy remain fixed.",
  "baseline": "Reuse the prior completed original CNN results after verifying their hashes; rerun original draw00 as an exact numerical control before new experiments.",
  "evaluation": "No evaluation labels in GPU learner. Freeze all predictions across the entire MNIST sweep before scoring. Freeze all extension predictions before scoring that stage. No early stopping or tuning after scores.",
  "backpropagation": "Store activations for ordinary exact backpropagation. Original input is explicitly retained in the first lifted channel; inverse checked independently. No reversible-memory claim.",
  "primary_sources": [
    "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.04585",
